language 0.1.0
module observability
  means
    Obtaining and presenting external evidence by which the internal execution
    and state of a running system can be judged.

entity signal : thing
  means
    signal: externally available evidence about the internal execution or
    state of a system.

entity log : thing
  means
    log record: a discrete structured signal about an event, formed at a
    definite moment.

entity metric : thing
  means
    metric: a named time series of numeric observations of a system.

entity trace : thing
  means
    trace: a connected representation of one operation passing through several
    stretches of execution.

entity span : thing
  means
    span: a time-bounded part of execution belonging to one trace.

entity alert : thing
  means
    alert: a signal that a given condition requiring attention or action has
    been met.

entity dashboard : thing
  means
    dashboard: an organised presentation of signals for judging the state of a
    system.
